/src/assets/art/

# Piper TTS voice models pulled down by `pnpm voice-over:setup` — a few hundred
# MB of binary ONNX, reproducible in one command from the casting table in
# `src/world/story/voices.ts`. The scratch WAVs the generator writes live in
# `tools/piper/_wav/` and are deleted at the end of every run.
tools/piper/

# NOTE: `public/speech/**` is deliberately NOT ignored. Those .ogg files are
# content, not build output: the hand-recorded lines live in the same folders as
# the generated placeholders and are indistinguishable from them on disk, so an
# ignore rule here would silently swallow the one kind of file nobody can
# regenerate. They also have to be in the repo for a platform build to contain
# any voice-over at all.

# Playwright
test-results/
playwright-report/
